      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the final price of the shirt after the two successive discounts, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the sale price after the first discount:**\n   The shirt is initially priced at $30 and is on sale for 20% off.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Amount of the first discount} = 30 \\times \\frac{20}{100} = 30 \\times 0.20 = 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sale price after the first discount} = 30 - 6 = 24\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the price after applying the coupon:**\n   Mary has a coupon that takes an additional 25% off the sale price.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Amount of the second discount} = 24 \\times \\frac{25}{100} = 24 \\times 0.25 = 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Final price after the second discount} = 24 - 6 = 18\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the final price as a percentage of the original price:**\n   The original price of the shirt is $30, and the final price is $18.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Final price as a percentage of the original price} = \\left( \\frac{18}{30} \\right) \\times 100 = 0.60 \\times 100 = 60\\%\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final price of the shirt after both discounts is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
